    "content": "1. **Architectural Drawing Production:** Clients submit initial architectural briefs; studio administrators assign projects to certified draughtsmen; draughtsmen produce and upload 2D CAD and BIM drawings.\n2. **Interactive Redline Reviews:** Clients and Engineers place pin annotations directly on drawing sheets to note dimension errors, structural clashes, or municipal zoning adjustments.\n3. **Controlled Revision Cycles:** Clients can request up to 3 correction rounds per milestone before granting final drawing approval.\n4. **Academy Drafting Curriculum:** Students progress through 12 structured drafting modules, submit practical CAD assignments, receive rubric-graded evaluations (≥ 80% passing threshold), and receive cryptographic SHA-256 verified certificates.\n5. **PIXMINT BOT:** A context-aware conversational AI assistant integrated across all portals to answer workflow questions, triage drawing issues, and guide users through procedures without compromising security."
